#! ia 1.0

@capability observation-method
  meaning
    says "Work with observation records under the IA methodology: the observation-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking an observation. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for an observation?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook observation-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook observation-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with observation records, each an attributed account of evidence with its interpretation and retention, whose claims field typing does not verify: orient through ia position --word observation and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with observation records?"
  subject
    subject-word observation
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word observation at the seat the work concerns, read the observation records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary observation --schema for the sections and fields an observation carries."
      Inference means "Read the observations left on the seat: who observed what, when, and how it was interpreted."
      Decision means "observation is a word of learning-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/learning-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these observation records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the observation must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Decide what the work will observe, and how each observation will be attributed and retained."
      Decision means "Extend an existing observation through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the observation will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the observation; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the observation with its attribution, evidence and interpretation, keeping what was seen apart from what it means."
      Decision means "Change observation records only through ia preview observation <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Check the observation against its evidence, and link it to any improvement it prompts."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the observation, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."

@capability improvement-method
  meaning
    says "Work with improvement records under the IA methodology: the improvement-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking an improvement. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for an improvement?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook improvement-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook improvement-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with improvement records, each a proposed change with review and publication metadata, which neither authorizes nor applies the change: orient through ia position --word improvement and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with improvement records?"
  subject
    subject-word improvement
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word improvement at the seat the work concerns, read the improvement records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary improvement --schema for the sections and fields an improvement carries."
      Inference means "Read the open improvements on the target and whether their digests still match its current text."
      Decision means "improvement is a word of learning-system: when the seat is not that system or a workspace that composes it, re-seat with ia position --seat floor/definition/system/learning-system before going on; its steward pointer is to read, not to invoke."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these improvement records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the improvement must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Name the target, its owning system and path, the exact text it replaces and that text's digest, the candidate, its verification and its reversal."
      Decision means "Extend an existing improvement through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the improvement will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the improvement; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Author the improvement as a proposal only; the target's owner reviews it and applies it."
      Decision means "Change improvement records only through ia preview improvement <name> <field>=<value>..., then ia author with the same form and the digest preview returned, then ia validate; use --set or --relate the same way for one field or relationship."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Treat a proposal whose target changed since its digest as stale: rebase it on the current text or withdraw it."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the improvement, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."
